      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "The vector $a$ has magnitude $8$, the vector $b$ has magnitude $3,$ the angle between $a$ and $b$ is ${85}^{∘}$ and $n$ is the unit vector that points in the direction of $a\\times b.$ Find $a\\times b$ in terms of $n.$ Round your final answer to one decimal place where appropriate.",
      "worked_solution": "We use the formula for the cross product and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|a|\\cdot |b|\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot n \\\\  & =8\\cdot 3\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{85}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\  & =24\\cdot (0.996\\,19…)\\cdot n \\\\  & =(23.908\\,67…)\\cdot n \\\\  & ≈23.9n.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
